ios: pointer robustness (one finger, pointercancel, canvas focus)

- Only one touch/pen pointer drives the canvas at a time: a second finger can no longer produce
  extra clicks, drags or camera moves (its events are ignored until it lifts). The filter tracks
  pointer ids instead of relying on e.isPrimary alone, because a finger resting on a host overlay
  button would make every later canvas touch non-primary; a primary pointerdown resets the tracking
  (self-heals after a lost pointerup).
- pointercancel (iOS takes the gesture over: Control Center, system gestures, ...) now releases
  everything: no click, drag emulation ended (an item drag is aborted, not dropped), camera pan
  ended, arrow keys released. Upstream had no pointercancel handler at all.
- pointerdown focuses the canvas (preventScroll) unless a text field has focus, so a hardware
  keyboard types into the game after a tap.

